    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0362" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg274"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-04-15"><hi rendition="#italic">April 15,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 25th of
                    November last, relative to certain alleged hardships suffered by the owners or
                    agents of British vessels arriving at the port of Boston with immigrants, I have
                    the honor to inclose a copy of a letter from the Acting Secretary of the
                    Treasury which sets forth the circumstances connected with the matter in
                    question, and states that the whole subject is now under consideration.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine</hi>.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d213-a1.xml" xpointer="d213-a1"/>
